# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in Go, compiled to a WebAssembly component
with [TinyGo](https://tinygo.org/) and packaged as `{{module_name}}.mpk`.
Scaffolded with `mpm-crate` — edit this project freely; it is a starting
point, not a generated artifact.

> **Experimental**: the Go guest toolchain is the newest of the five guest
> languages and has had the least mileage. Expect rough edges.

It defines three tables (`items`, `item_info`, `item_info_labels`, see
`sql/ddl.sql`) and two Mudu Procedures (see `procedures.go`):
`create_item` (scalar arguments) and `update_item_info`, which demonstrates
a **user-defined record type** — the `item-info` record declared in
`wit/types.wit` — as a procedure parameter and return type.

## Prerequisites

On PATH:

- **TinyGo 0.42.0** (`tinygo`) — the compiler.
  Install the linux-amd64 (or darwin) tarball from
  <https://github.com/tinygo-org/tinygo/releases/tag/v0.42.0> and put its
  `bin/` on PATH; override the binary with
  `TINYGO=/path/to/tinygo cargo make`.
- **Go 1.27.1** (`go`) — required by TinyGo itself, which shells out to
  the `go` command for package loading on every build (this is a TinyGo
  constraint, not something this project can opt out of). Install the
  tarball from <https://go.dev/dl/> and put its `bin/` on PATH.
- `wasm-tools` (`cargo install wasm-tools`) and `cargo-make` (`cargo
  install cargo-make`).
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain; `mpm-install`,
  `mudud`, `mcli` to install and invoke the package.

Builds run **offline**: the wit-bindgen-go output under `binding/` is
checked in and both Go module dependencies are vendored under `vendor/` —
the `go.bytecodealliance.org/cm v0.3.0` component-model runtime and the
`github.com/ybbh/mududb_p/bindings/go` wire library (packages `types` +
`codec`: the Uni* types/MSSP codecs and the record bridge) — so no module
ever downloads. The bindings were produced with `wit-bindgen-go` v0.7.0
(`go run go.bytecodealliance.org/cmd/wit-bindgen-go@v0.7.0`).

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `procedures.go` — hand-written procedures; SQL runs through
  `mudusys.go` (MSSP framing) over the `mududb:api/system` byte pipe.
  Each procedure is a func with a `// mudu-proc` comment immediately above
  it; the first parameter is the `muduOid` session, the result a
  `(T, error)` pair. Parameter and result types: `int64` (I64), `string`
  (String), `float64` (F64), `bool` (I32), `[]byte` (Binary), and the
  user-defined record types of `wit/types.wit` (used as
  `gentypes.ItemInfo`).
- `wit/types.wit` — the project's message types (the `item-info` record),
  consumed two ways: `mgen message` turns it into the Go structs/codecs of
  the `gentypes` package, and `mtp --type-wit` registers the names so
  procedure signatures may use them. The `package` clause is required: one
  WIT directory is one package, and the TinyGo world build rejects
  headerless files sitting next to a packaged world.
- `gentypes/` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make gentypes`): the
  `ItemInfo` struct plus its `ItemInfoToValue`/`ItemInfoFromValue` codecs
  (`types.go`) and the helper runtime they reference (`wire.go`). Never
  edit by hand.
- `<table>.go` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make generate`, from
  `sql/ddl.sql`): one `package main` file per table — the `<Table>Row`
  struct, the row codec and the typed `Insert` / `Get<Table>ByPk` /
  `Delete<Table>ByPk` helpers the procedures build on. Nullable columns
  are pointer fields (nil means SQL NULL). Never edit by hand.
- `main_gen.go` — **generated by mtp** (`cargo make transpile`): the
  `package main` wiring module — one `Exports.Mp2<PascalProc>` assignment
  per procedure (decode the wire parameters with the `asXxx` helpers of
  `mudusys.go` — record parameters through the binding bridge
  `types.RecordFieldValues` composed with `gentypes.ItemInfoFromValue` —
  dispatch, encode the result), the shared `invoke` driver, and an empty
  `main`. Never edit by hand.
- `mpack.go` — the minimal MessagePack codec the wire format needs.
- `binding/` — wit-bindgen-go output for the mtp-generated
  `wit/world.wit`, checked in so builds need only TinyGo ("Code generated
  by wit-bindgen-go. DO NOT EDIT." — regenerate with `cargo make
  regen-bindings`).
- `vendor/` — the vendored Go module dependencies (see Prerequisites).
- `wit/world.wit` — **generated by mtp**: the component world, `include
  wasi:cli/imports` (the WASI 0.2 interfaces the TinyGo runtime needs;
  unused ones are pruned from the component) plus `import
  mududb:api/system` and one `mp2-<kebab-proc>` export per procedure.
  `wit/deps/mududb-api/api.wit` is a copy of the host syscall interface;
  `wit/deps/cli|clocks|io|...` are the upstream WASI 0.2.0 interface
  definitions shipped with TinyGo.
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata.
- `package/package.desc.json` — **generated by mtp**: the procedure
  signatures. camelCase function and parameter names normalize to the
  snake_case wire form (`createItem` → `create_item`, `itemID` →
  `item_id`); a record parameter is described with the host's `Record`
  type family, the WIT field names verbatim as the JSON keys.

Adding a procedure means writing the func plus its `// mudu-proc` marker
and rebuilding — the wiring, the world WIT and the descriptor stay in
sync because all three come from the same source. The Go-only extra step:
the checked-in bindings under `binding/` are generated from the world, so
after adding or renaming procedures run `cargo make regen-bindings` once
(the first run downloads the wit-bindgen-go tool; plain builds never
touch the network).

## Records on the wire

A record argument travels as the positional `uni-data-value` record case
(field order = WIT declaration order, names dropped by the host); the
guest side never touches that envelope by hand — the mtp-generated
adapter decodes it through the binding record bridge composed with the
mgen-generated codec, and encodes a record result symmetrically. Rules of
the JSON/desc surface:

- **JSON keys = WIT field names, verbatim** (`in-stock`, not `inStock`).
- **Booleans cross as 0/1** — the host has no boolean data-type family, so
  a WIT `bool` field is described as `I32` and takes JSON `0`/`1`.
- **u32/u16/u8 fields cross as i32**; missing JSON fields are an error,
  unknown keys are tolerated.

`update_item_info` stores the record flattened into the `item_info` table
(the label list as `item_info_labels` side rows keyed by `(item_id,
idx)`), updating the row by key and inserting it on first write.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` (generate) → `mgen check-sql` → `mgen message`
(gentypes) → `mtp go` (transpile) → `tinygo build -target=wasip2`
(compile → componentize) → `wasm-tools validate` → `mpm-build create`,
producing `target/wasip2/{{module_name}}.mpk`. The component file is named
`{{module_name}}.wasm` so its stem matches the `{{module_name}}` module in
`package/package.desc.json` (an `mpm-build` requirement).

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/wasip2/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'

# the record procedure: nested JSON, WIT field names verbatim, bool as 0/1
mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc update_item_info \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "info": {"name": "pear", "price": 199, "in-stock": 1, "labels": ["fresh", "green"]}}'
```
